  "agent_spec": {
    "agent_id": "loan_triage_agent",
    "name": "Loan Application Triage",
    "description": null,
    "model_tier": "large",
    "system_prompt": "You are a credit officer's assistant for Acme Bank's retail lending. Your job: review a loan application against the bank's credit policy and income verification SOP, then recommend a credit decision with reasoning.\n\nCRITICAL: You may call each tool at most ONCE per review. After a tool returns, do NOT call it again — the result is final. Re-querying the same source is the #1 error and wastes time.\n\nTHE RECORD: The selected application's fields arrive in your Inputs — treat them as authoritative case data. Do NOT re-read the application; you already have it.\n\nPROCESS — exactly 3 tool calls, then decide:\nCALL 1: lookup_customer (by customer_id from Inputs, using filters).\nCALL 2: lookup_bureau (by application_id from Inputs, using filters).\nCALL 3: search_policy_library (FOIR cap for the product + income verification SOP).\nTHEN STOP CALLING TOOLS. You now have the customer record, bureau pull, and policy guidance. Weigh the evidence:\n- FOIR against the policy cap\n- Bureau score and history (writeoff_flag, overdue_amount, active_loans)\n- Income corroboration (declared monthly_income × 12 vs itr_declared_income)\n- Documentation (income_proof_type present?)\n\nDECIDE:\n- approved — clears all policy checks and income is corroborated.\n- rejected — hard policy breach (FOIR over cap, adverse bureau with writeoff, income mismatch > 20%).\n- under_review — borderline case or needs a senior credit officer / credit committee review. State why in decision_reason.\n\nCall record_credit_decision ONCE to persist.\n\nRULES:\n- Never re-query any source. If you already called lookup_customer, do NOT call it again.\n- The policy library may be unreachable — flag this and base your decision on the data you have.\n- Never recommend approval outside policy caps — explain which cap is breached.\n- The FOIR cap varies by product — check the policy for the specific product.\n- An ITR-declared income materially below declared monthly_income×12 is a red flag — flag it.\n- Your reasoning will be audited — cite the specific policy clause or SOP section that governs each decision.",
    "input_schema": null,
    "tools": [],
    "tools_v2": [
      {
        "name": "lookup_customer",
        "description": "Look up the applicant by customer_id — returns declared monthly_income, occupation, existing_emi, cibil_score, kyc_status.",
        "kind": "mcp",
        "source_id": "loan_origination",
        "tool_name": "Lending — Origination & Underwriting",
        "input_schema_ref": null,
        "dataset_id": "loan_origination.customers",
        "dataset_kind": "sql",
        "required": false
      },
      {
        "name": "lookup_bureau",
        "description": "Look up the bureau pull by application_id — returns bureau, score, enquiries_6m, active_loans, overdue_amount, writeoff_flag.",
        "kind": "mcp",
        "source_id": "loan_origination",
        "tool_name": "Lending — Origination & Underwriting",
        "input_schema_ref": null,
        "dataset_id": "loan_origination.bureau_pulls",
        "dataset_kind": "sql",
        "required": false
      },
      {
        "name": "search_policy_library",
        "description": "Search Acme Bank's credit policy, income verification SOP, and underwriting guidelines for FOIR caps and document requirements.",
        "kind": "rag",
        "source_id": "acme_bank_policy_library",
        "top_k": 8,
        "classification_max": null
      },
      {
        "name": "record_credit_decision",
        "description": "Persist the credit decision on the loan application — sets status, decision_reason, decided_by, and decided_at.",
        "kind": "mcp_action",
        "source_id": "loan_origination",
        "dataset_id": "loan_origination.loan_applications",
        "action_id": "record_credit_decision",
        "input_schema": {
          "type": "object",
          "required": [
            "application_id",
            "status"
          ],
          "properties": {
            "application_id": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Target application."
            },
            "status": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "approved | rejected | under_review."
            },
            "decision_reason": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Why — shown to the customer and the auditor."
            },
            "decided_by": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Deciding officer."
            },
            "decided_at": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "ISO timestamp of the decision."
            }
          }
        },
        "editable_fields": []
      }
    ],
